\
### Bayesian workflow and model validation \
- We conducted an extensive, iterative model refinement process (the Bayesian Workflow) outlined in Gelman et al. 2020: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.01808"}}{\fldrslt https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.01808}})\
- Step 1: Consideration and refinement of domain knowledge\
	- why and how would food waste get eaten by American Crows? See full process here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://miro.com/welcomeonboard/THREVjRuVFNLUGdZbjc5RzFJbXJnUGdPSUVDM29aZ0JNZEUrVUVIT2ZGZGkzc1U4WER3dXV6UU9tM2RmZWdOTGJyRzhhM252MlhCR04wRForMUxlZ1lHNWVITFpZRVZRbmFkemRqTFdxN2Jnc2ZNcFNtMk1HQW9YOWErSVMxYURnbHpza3F6REdEcmNpNEFOMmJXWXBBPT0hdjE=?share_link_id=508155194688"}}{\fldrslt https://miro.com/welcomeonboard/THREVjRuVFNLUGdZbjc5RzFJbXJnUGdPSUVDM29aZ0JNZEUrVUVIT2ZGZGkzc1U4WER3dXV6UU9tM2RmZWdOTGJyRzhhM252MlhCR04wRForMUxlZ1lHNWVITFpZRVZRbmFkemRqTFdxN2Jnc2ZNcFNtMk1HQW9YOWErSVMxYURnbHpza3F6REdEcmNpNEFOMmJXWXBBPT0hdjE=?share_link_id=508155194688}}\
	- specifically, what kinds of food waste exist?\
	- what changes how much there is?\
	- what determines how accessible it is to crows?\
- Step 2: Translating domain knowledge into initial model structure hypothesis\
- Step 3: Simulate data from hypothesized model\
- Step 4: Develop priors, run prior predictive checks (do my priors make sense?)\
- Step 5: Run this model on empirical data\
- Step 6: Run retrodictive (i.e., posterior predictive) checks to evaluate fit\
	- We primarily determined the goodness of fit using posterior predictive checks (visually comparing distribution of the simulated data to observations)\
	- This involves plotting density distribution from 50 (or more) draws from the posterior distribution from our model on top of the empirical data\
		- do they match well? If not, where? Why might that be? Could we have used a better distribution, should we change our predictors, etc.?\
	- Look at Rhat values\
- Step 7: Start back at the step where you think improvements could be made (usually Step 2 or later)\
- Optional Step 8: use leave-one-out cross-validation and/or WAIC to compare model performance\
